From cc11fa176925397890647ad7ea86e72f350f58be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:14:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/22] sheet surface: fix three census failure mechanisms at
 the source

Population census (2009 cells, production preset) failed on four cut cells;
each was diagnosed and fixed in the mesher rather than excluded:

- snap_near_plane_constrained: the joint correction that keeps a vertex on
  the planes it already lies on projected face vertices near a shallow cut
  plane onto the intersection line, a move of eps/sin(theta) along the face
  (19 snap distances at 3 deg).  This folded the boundary strip, stranded
  vertices off the level set (residuals up to 0.3) and even pulled sheet
  from the removed wedge into the retained region.  The correction is now
  capped at 2 eps; farther vertices are left to the exact clip.
- cap boundary polygon: a port face without carrier constraints used the
  whole cube face, so on a face crossed by the cut the flood fill leaked past
  the cut line.  Every cap now uses the facet of the retained region
  (_retained_facet_polygon).
- tangent patches: sheet triangles within h/2 of a plane with material in
  between were partly snapped, pinching the sheet onto the cap along an
  interior edge (four triangles on one edge).  _flatten_tangent_patches
  snaps such patches as a whole so the flat-triangle drop removes them and
  the cap closes the solid.

Two unit tests added (snap cap, facet polygon); 12 tests pass.  The four
cells and a 20-cell regression panel build watertight surfaces and volumes.
